  "notes": "No new CSS syntax is added; this Chrome 159 change updates how existing AccentColor and AccentColorText <system-color> keywords resolve against the element's computed accent-color property. Pre-existing OS-level system color rollout is documented at /v150/accentcolor-and-accentcolortext-system-colors/ and on MDN. All resolution, cycle-breaking, animation, and forced-colors rules trace directly to CSS Color 4 §6.2, CSS UI 4 §7.1, CSS Color Adjustment 1, and the five landed WPT test files."
